  "_appPages_comment": [
    "The app's own pages (card 472). The \"Graph ready\" chip opens the code graph",
    "through the server that runs the app, at /api/codegraph/view, which serves",
    "the folder's graph.html under a CSP sandbox. That page passes without the",
    "loopback opt-in only with a ticket: the server mints one when the operator",
    "presses the chip, it lives for one minute, and the view spends it on the",
    "first load. `ticket` is the one ticket the fence knows to be live (null:",
    "none). The shape is exact: http, a loopback host (localhost, 127.0.0.1 or",
    "[::1]), the port the app's server listens on (`appPort`; 0 means not known),",
    "no userinfo, the path exactly as listed, and exactly one `ticket` parameter",
    "whose value is live. An agent's verbs never carry a live ticket, so the view",
    "keeps the loopback rule for them, as every other loopback address does."
  ],
